'''Stock''', sometimes called '''bone broth''', is a savory cooking liquid that forms the basis of many [[Dish (food)|dishes]] {{ndash}} particularly [[soup]]s, [[stew]]s, and [[sauce]]s. Making stock involves simmering animal bones, meat, seafood, or vegetables in water or wine, often for an extended period. [[Mirepoix (cuisine)|Mirepoix]] or other aromatics may be added for more flavor.
